    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d807">

                <pb facs="1251" n="1225" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg1225"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/6–2254: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the United States Delegation</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d807-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-06-23T11:20:00-04:00">June 23, 1954—11:20
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Tosec 464. Limit distribution. Ref Secto 501.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d807-f2"/>
                    Chauvel‘s evasiveness re “underground
                    military talks” is contrary our understanding with him and Mendes-France that we were to be kept fully
                    informed.</p>
                <p>Suggest Johnson take earliest appropriate
                    occasion remind Chauvel this understanding
                    and to add that our continued presence at Geneva can be useful only to the
                    degree that we are in fact kept fully informed.</p>
                <p>Ambassador Dillon should make similar
                    representations Mendes-France.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d807-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d807-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Sturm of FE/PSA. Sent to Paris as telegram
                    4756 and repeated to Saigon as telegram 2698.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d807-f2" n="2" xml:id="d807-f2-content">
                <p>Dated June 22, <ref target="#pg1222">p. 1222</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
